"7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186210486} {:answer/id #uuid "59b45d2d-1c4c-573d-9659-1f20d0a48e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186210487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7f652a1-09b5-5d26-9d6d-4b17464cb624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186210483} :answer-field/id #uuid "66636cdc-19cb-516d-87a2-e60beff64fb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186210482}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20af0bb2-503a-581b-8ca0-14bdc38233bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-288055" :question/problem "The equation\n$k(x^{2} + 7x + 10) = 5x^{2} + 35x + 50$\n\nis true for all values of $x$, where $k$ is a constant. What is the value of $k$?" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means that after distributing $k$ on the left-hand side, the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nk({x}^{2}+7x+10)=k{x}^{2}+7kx+10k\n$$\n\nThis must equal the right-hand side. So, we have\n\n$$\nk{x}^{2}+7kx+10k=5{x}^{2}+35x+50.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms. \n\nComparing the ${x}^{2}$ terms, we have\n\n$$\nk=5.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that value $k=5$ produces the correct linear coefficient and constant term:\n\n- $7k=7(5)=35\\,✓$\n\n- $10k=10(5)=50\\,✓$\n\nSo, our solution is valid."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186213381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "46822f28-8863-5150-a420-09c61a5c28b1" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing Factored Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ebcf35-bbf4-510e-b778-b3168bd4ab49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232686} {:answer/id #uuid "67d06be6-5ae9-5aa9-9041-9034eeac2a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9ebcf35-bbf4-510e-b778-b3168bd4ab49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232686} :answer-field/id #uuid "481eeb6a-9808-5dae-8221-c828106cd034" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186210488}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "727fbc37-51b3-52b0-84e6-bde484330ac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-288057" :question/problem "The equation\n$(ax + 4)(x + b) = 2x^{2} + 14x + 20$\n\nis true for all values of $x$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants. What is the value of $a + b$?\n\n$a + b =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ax+4)(x+b) & =a{x}^{2}+abx+4x+4b \\\\  & =a{x}^{2}+(ab+4)x+4b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\na{x}^{2}+(ab+4)x+4b=2{x}^{2}+14x+20.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\na=2.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n4b=20\\,⇒\\,b=5.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $a=2$ and $b=5$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ab+4 & =2\\cdot 5+4 \\\\  & =10+4 \\\\  & =14\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $a+b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =2+5 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5cf64df7-0abb-5b42-bed6-b3664c2de89a" :knowledge-point/title "Matching a Single Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64193841-37e5-5f6f-b7b6-ee80ea70ef7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255499} {:answer/id #uuid "5df47a74-45ac-526c-a005-e428f82aec18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255500} {:answer/id #uuid "89116d43-736f-58e1-b2f9-ebb01b88dc2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255501} {:answer/id #uuid "034d4eaf-acd8-5aeb-b833-e47db369a479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255502} {:answer/id #uuid "5a6796a7-100b-575c-89cb-569553035214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "034d4eaf-acd8-5aeb-b833-e47db369a479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255502} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0782702-574b-500d-ab07-bd7521937c96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255498}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d83f702-a7b0-525f-b516-fc34f6f27759" :question/math-academy-id "q-288406" :question/problem "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}+mx-6=-5{x}^{2}-3x-6\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $m?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the linear terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $m.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $-3.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nm=-3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5cf64df7-0abb-5b42-bed6-b3664c2de89a" :knowledge-point/title "Matching a Single Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b7d2d19-dcd0-5314-b8b5-9fa26a34a163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255506} {:answer/id #uuid "53aefaef-b653-5988-a27e-e1a4f42ff66b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255507} {:answer/id #uuid "564bcc95-65a5-57d6-ae71-9e51a6c72a30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255508} {:answer/id #uuid "a3c09eb4-ee0b-5c3d-8a53-cdbeab73b38e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255509} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b3d4ab-51fe-51ae-a51b-fe3135765567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b7d2d19-dcd0-5314-b8b5-9fa26a34a163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255506} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf96108-0f92-59da-b703-00689fe8dd10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255505}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3063c6de-d529-5ec7-be38-9576a5bfefab" :question/math-academy-id "q-288446" :question/problem "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-7x+n=4{x}^{2}-7x+2\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $n?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the constant terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the constant is $n.$ On the right-hand side, the constant is $2.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nn=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5cf64df7-0abb-5b42-bed6-b3664c2de89a" :knowledge-point/title "Matching a Single Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90b98ad6-0d26-5417-8a5f-23b1652dfcd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255513} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d68d17-b4d2-5609-8bc9-032941933f05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8d68d17-b4d2-5609-8bc9-032941933f05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255514} :answer-field/id #uuid "0badedaf-efa3-504f-a7fa-bec469764e32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255512}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77bcd568-42e4-5b14-ad02-144823509fd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-288448" :question/problem "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\nk{x}^{2}+4x+1=-2{x}^{2}+4x+1\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the quadratic terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is $k.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is $-2.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nk=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2caeb2c-39cf-595a-8105-67d11bf0e45e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57944513-f089-57e2-be4e-82a4b018a3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255517} {:answer/id #uuid "43dc81ee-bed2-503a-80f5-c72f17768141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255518} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc5e965-e4a9-5e2a-8e1f-4994b8aedee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255519} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f94a06-911d-5ead-a5ae-2c35a7696751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255520} {:answer/id #uuid "1a5845ce-6ea2-5030-9a3c-a63935aca909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cc5e965-e4a9-5e2a-8e1f-4994b8aedee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255519} :answer-field/id #uuid "070d8ebc-e2b3-5395-ac7c-f602cb2a9ae5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255516}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbe86354-6280-5067-a456-42950cdfd26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-288451" :question/problem "The equation \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+mx+c={x}^{2}+7x-5\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $m$ and $c$ are constants. What is the value of $m+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $m,$ and on the right-hand side it is $7.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nm=7.\n$$\n\n- The constant term on the left-hand side is $c,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-5.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nc=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+c & =7+(-5) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2caeb2c-39cf-595a-8105-67d11bf0e45e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed785341-1301-5e9b-9415-bead8f0dabb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255524} {:answer/id #uuid "808d3963-90f8-5ac1-89d7-d1deec77ecb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255525} {:answer/id #uuid "58af5c1a-841f-598d-b82c-121c30f8d6a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255526} {:answer/id #uuid "be4d0d45-11b5-5356-9466-d79c1bc36ba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255527} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea4fedd-c176-5516-bcb4-6c73de21c793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed785341-1301-5e9b-9415-bead8f0dabb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255524} :answer-field/id #uuid "73dbd387-dbc2-5a93-b8c2-e40bad3c1830" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255523}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef6fd5d3-be04-5074-a0a6-cef98c8ae090" :question/math-academy-id "q-288452" :question/problem "The equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+nx+d={x}^{2}-12x-8\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $n$ and $d$ are constants. What is the value of $n+d?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $n,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-12.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nn=-12.\n$$\n\n- The constant term on the left-hand side is $d,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-8.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nd=-8.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n+d & =-12+(-8) \\\\  & =-12-8 \\\\  & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2caeb2c-39cf-595a-8105-67d11bf0e45e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b25085bc-40ff-5d1d-943f-e31268f4f786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255531} {:answer/id #uuid "8704a721-176a-5207-bda6-5d4b11b46933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8704a721-176a-5207-bda6-5d4b11b46933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255532} :answer-field/id #uuid "652da9b8-4c2c-59b4-ae35-d86b5193ef15" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255530}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a6c0692-e234-5b82-adb2-8a6dc6c8405c" :question/math-academy-id "q-288459" :question/problem "The equation\n\n$$\np{x}^{2}+qx-6={x}^{2}+7x-6\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $p$ and $q$ are constants. What is the value of $pq?$\n\n$pq=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ on the left-hand side is $p,$ and on the right-hand side it is $1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\np=1.\n$$\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $q,$ and on the right-hand side it is $7.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nq=7.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}pq & =1\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2caeb2c-39cf-595a-8105-67d11bf0e45e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091e819b-931a-5249-a7c7-1e8e48b61bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "091e819b-931a-5249-a7c7-1e8e48b61bf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255535} :answer-field/id #uuid "01b097be-48a0-541a-9ca5-94f86b8fbc0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255534}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e44f0762-0d97-57a0-af00-2ff5a26957f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-288463" :question/problem "The equation\n\n$$\nt{x}^{2}+wx+6=4{x}^{2}-2x+6\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $t$ and $w$ are constants. What is the value of $tw?$\n\n$tw=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ on the left-hand side is $t,$ and on the right-hand side it is $4.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nt=4.\n$$\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $w,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-2.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nw=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tw & =4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2caeb2c-39cf-595a-8105-67d11bf0e45e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c4440ff-6fcf-5796-8092-e168dfb8d9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c4440ff-6fcf-5796-8092-e168dfb8d9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1888d438-714b-5154-b9be-b524b7304b1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255537}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b996e1b8-0371-5d56-a6f0-f9cbd6e51c66" :question/math-academy-id "q-288464" :question/problem "The equation \n\n$$\nu{x}^{2}+vx-3=-7{x}^{2}+x-3\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $u$ and $v$ are constants. What is the value of $uv?$\n\n$uv=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ on the left-hand side is $u,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-7.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nu=-7.\n$$\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $v,$ and on the right-hand side it is $1.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nv=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}uv & =(-7)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "46822f28-8863-5150-a420-09c61a5c28b1" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing Factored Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c8222b-75e0-5775-84d3-f1224424ed81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255541} {:answer/id #uuid "dd68e33a-5c52-5923-97ab-e722a61e4fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255542} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbe5945-bfff-52d7-a503-35996d529bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255543} {:answer/id #uuid "9e55d357-4249-5383-84bb-727fa1e29284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255544} {:answer/id #uuid "f4545191-d3a5-58f8-8bd2-c496a9006f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4545191-d3a5-58f8-8bd2-c496a9006f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255545} :answer-field/id #uuid "daebb1a6-92f0-59cf-bff5-b5367267f8bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255540}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f05ef00-ecf3-521e-8eb7-f45de3139297" :question/math-academy-id "q-288468" :question/problem "The equation\n\n$$\nt(2{x}^{2}-3x+1)=-6{x}^{2}+9x-3\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $t$ is a constant. What is the value of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means that after distributing $t$ on the left-hand side, the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\nt(2{x}^{2}-3x+1)=2t{x}^{2}-3tx+t\n$$\n\nThis must equal the right-hand side. So, we have\n\n$$\n2t{x}^{2}-3tx+t=-6{x}^{2}+9x-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms. \n\nComparing the ${x}^{2}$ terms, we have\n\n$$\n2t=-6\\,⇒\\,t=-3.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that value $t=-3$ produces the correct linear coefficient and constant term:\n\n- $-3t=(-3)(-3)=9\\,✓$\n\n- $t=-3\\,✓$\n\nSo, our solution is valid."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "46822f28-8863-5150-a420-09c61a5c28b1" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing Factored Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f0e7d6d-7f8f-5fc4-b1b6-a416d2781d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f0e7d6d-7f8f-5fc4-b1b6-a416d2781d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255548} :answer-field/id #uuid "6164c4c1-c223-5f65-b959-f84fc20d982f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255547}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c020a0c1-43c7-514c-b47c-f3c429e8e8cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-288697" :question/problem "The equation \n\n$$\n(cx-8)(x+d)=4{x}^{2}-20x+24\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $c$ and $d$ are constants.What is the value of $c+d?$\n\n$c+d=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(cx-8)(x+d) & =c{x}^{2}+cdx-8x-8d \\\\  & =c{x}^{2}+(cd-8)x-8d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nc{x}^{2}+(cd-8)x-8d=4{x}^{2}-20x+24.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\nc=4.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n-8d=24\\,⇒\\,d=-3.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $c=4$ and $d=-3$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cd-8 & =4\\cdot (-3)-8 \\\\  & =-12-8 \\\\  & =-20\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $c+d:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c+d & =4+(-3) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "46822f28-8863-5150-a420-09c61a5c28b1" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing Factored Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63f7f2c9-d41a-5f88-8548-80aefb6d7627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63f7f2c9-d41a-5f88-8548-80aefb6d7627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255551} :answer-field/id #uuid "78b6324b-22fe-5284-8b6c-f377ca83ad25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255550}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e2b02957-533e-54ac-94ee-103972717b02" :question/math-academy-id "q-288698" :question/problem "The equation\n\n$$\n(mx+10)(x+n)=-5{x}^{2}+20x-20\n$$\n\nis true for all values of $x,$ where $m$ and $n$ are constants. What is the value of $m+n?$\n\n$m+n=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the product on the left-hand side must expand to match the right-hand side.\n\nFirst, let's expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(mx+10)(x+n) & =m{x}^{2}+mnx+10x+10n \\\\  & =m{x}^{2}+(mn+10)x+10n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we equate the expanded form to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nm{x}^{2}+(mn+10)x+10n=-5{x}^{2}+20x-20.\n$$\n\nNow, we compare the coefficients of corresponding terms.\n\n- Equating the coefficients of ${x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\nm=-5.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constant terms, we get\n\n$$\n10n=-20\\,⇒\\,n=-2.\n$$\n\nLet's verify that values $m=-5$ and $n=-2$ produce the correct linear coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}mn+10 & =(-5)(-2)+10 \\\\  & =10+10 \\\\  & =20\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the coefficient of $x$ on the right-hand side. So, our solution is valid.\n\nFinally, we compute the value of $m+n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+n & =-5+(-2) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
